    "adopted_policy": "# P212 plain-build V3: root source reception and explicit replacement policy\n\n2026-09-11 UTC. ACCEPT_SOURCE_AND_NEW_BRANCH_POLICY; NO_BUILD_GRANT.\nThis is root integration, not independent manuscript review or a completed\npaper. P211/P213 remain complete; P212 remains incomplete. HOLD_EXTERNAL.\n\n## Evidence received\n\nRoot read the project workflow/current anchor and inherited authorization\nand artifact contract, the original S0 reception/dependency gate/seventeen\nconsumer delta, and the bounded replacement diagnosis. Root read all eight\nV3 proposed document bodies, the full source diff, complete 163-line recipe,\nrequest, contract, handoff, V2/V3 diff and resource diagnosis. The latter's\n14,813 bytes have SHA256\n7c930faacf506bae17a6d49d3dff26e1587d972e25b31794b5542b1b4304daae.\nThe whole selected 223-row P213 manifest and its ordinary-trust handoff were\nread as archival documents, not followed as host paths.\n\nRoot strict 21f448 passed all 26 proposal payloads. Actual cdbe0d compared\nall eight V2/V3 proposed pairs and current-live/V3-original pairs as full\nraw bytes. The proposed eight total 20,165 bytes versus original 20,092;\nonly main's preamble and five table presentation substitutions change.\nSix files, all formulas/proofs/cells and all five bibliography entries are\nunchanged. This is source invariance, not a fresh proof or layout verdict.\n\nRoot read both complete independent DATA checkers before executing them.\nActual d017d2 and 08ecb5 both exit 0; full native requests/results are\npreserved here in V2_DATA_REPLAY_NATIVE.json and V3_DATA_REPLAY_NATIVE.json.\nActual 19d007 compares their entire outputs with independent 9ad3f5 and\nba1042: 9,643 and 15,829 bytes respectively, both raw equal. The record is\nPAIR_COMPARISON_NATIVE.json. This is a documentary replay, not execution\nof any proposed build script. V3 checks complete package contents, exact\nwhole diffs, request settings and the archival resource/config comparison.\n\nThe [independent review](../p212_plain_build_source_audit01/REVIEW.md) and\n[staged supplement](../p212_plain_build_source_audit01/STAGED_POLICY_SUPPLEMENT.md)\nwere read completely, including the final resource clarification. Actual\na0eb4c passed the independent six-payload seal. The independent reviewer\nhas no authorship of this build proposal or mathematical content; related\nprior audit work is disclosed, not blind or external review. No A/B credit.\n\nOne root metadata-inspection command 2dbcc6 failed by treating the scalar\nscope field as a request record. It made no mutation; 88b325 and 9055c3\nthen read the actual scope/record keys and complete request arguments.\nThe independent navigation/display and patch-context failures remain in\nits original package. None is a build success or an omitted scientific run.\n\n## Explicit root policy adoption\n\nRoot now adopts the exact proposal03 CONTRACT.md together with the staged\nsupplement (SHA256 055b06bc5e47ffa1fd6459101e473c86808fbfe44a2d56f186012efb9fa2f1b3).\nThe supplement has precedence over HANDOFF line 7, request line 48 and any\nunqualified S6 reading requiring a future cold directory to have been\nobserved before it is created. P212-POLICY-TIME1 is therefore CLOSED only\nfor this combined new policy. The frozen V3 wording and finding remain.\nCurrent combined SOURCE/POLICY findings: 0 Critical / 0 Major / 0 Minor open.\n\nThis new ordinary-build branch trusts Bash/env, fixed installed tools and\nconfiguration, filesystem/namespace ancestors and transport in precisely\nthe disclosed ordinary sense. All seventeen old consumer dispositions are\nadopted for this branch only. The uncalled kpsewhich/driver/preload/native14\ninterfaces and strict source/init/descendant claims are retired-not-invoked\nor withdrawn here, never PASS under their old contracts. Old B1–B4, old\nfailed evidence, captured DATA and consumed grants are not altered. No new\nquery/ELF/package/source observer is required for an absent interface.\n\nRoot accepts the resource diagnosis as a finite prospective selection\nargument: no demonstrated new uncovered consumer or required font basename\nwas found after removing the explicit small-table choice. The exact 223\nshared candidates may form P212's new selected manifest, with current full\ncontent revalidation and the same thirteen-variable configuration binding\nbefore grant. This is not exhaustive font/native/Fontconfig/cache closure,\nnot a transfer of P213's artifact constants, and not yet a current key.\nThe existing format is trusted/pinned, not rebuilt or falsely proved from\ncurrent latex.ltx. Any known concrete missing consumer must be resolved\nbefore build; an unknown actual FLS input stops later acceptance.\n\nA future separate grant may authorize exactly one conditional staged V3\ncommand: first exclusive construction/copy/key checks and actual cwd/member\nguard; TeX/BibTeX/rendering only after all of those and product absences\nactually succeed. Root receives current global keys and the exact output\nparent beforehand, not fabricated future-cwd observations. Guard failure\npreserves partial evidence and stops. Root must later receive the complete\nactual cwd/member record and transport, not merely a success marker.\nThe new policy explicitly permits ordinary /dev/null redirection and the\nreviewed 600/180-second timeouts with TERM and 10-second kill-after. Early\nnative failures cannot acquire invented controller exits. Only a genuinely\nreturned session may be continued; no automatic second launch or retry.\n\n## Next authorized preparation, not build\n\nApply exactly the two received presentation deltas to live only after\npreserving/comparing their old bytes; recheck all eight against the received\nmanifest. Prepare a new P212 selected runtime manifest from the identified\n223 candidates and perform a bounded current hash check of those exact\npaths under ordinary tool trust. Receive the fixed output parent and current\ncapacity before substantial output; create only necessary new workspace\npreparation directories. Bind exact recipe/request/source/runtime/policy\nbytes externally before a separate consumed one-build grant. This receipt\ndoes not execute or authorize the build command itself.\n\nActual full logs, ordered FLS including duplicates/generated chronology,\nAUX-before-BibTeX/BLG/BBL and five-key reconciliation, fonts/text/glyphs,\nactual page count and every actual page view remain mandatory. No P213\ncounts/PDF/review/canonical are copied as P212 results. Round0, nonauthor\nA/B, deltas/freezes, required exact science pairs and two terminal builds\nare still later gates. Existing accepted author science is not restarted\nfor a presentation-only edit; any later reuse retains its actual dependency\nscope. Finish only the current five-paper batch and scoped private sync.\n",
    "staged_supplement": "# P212 V3: independent staged-policy clarification\n\nStatus: SOURCE-REVIEWED SUPPLEMENT FOR EXPLICIT ROOT ADOPTION. This document\nis not a grant, resource receipt, actual-cwd observation or build result.\nThe frozen proposal01/02/03 packages remain unchanged.\n\n## Exact documentary issue and precedence\n\nFinding P212-POLICY-TIME1, Minor documentary timing inconsistency: proposal03\n[HANDOFF.md line 7](../p212_plain_build_source_proposal03/HANDOFF.md) requires\nactual-cwd configuration before issuing any build grant, and\n[NATIVE_REQUEST.proposed.json line 48](../p212_plain_build_source_proposal03/NATIVE_REQUEST.proposed.json)\nplaces actual-cwd reception before grant. But the exact proposed recipe\ncreates COLD at lines 22–24 and obtains its actual guard evidence only at\nlines 53–91, during that same separately granted command. Its first TeX\ninvocation is at line 135. Future-directory observation cannot be asserted\nbefore this construction occurs.\n\nThe following staged meaning is sufficient to resolve the inconsistency\nwithout changing frozen source or adding another observer. Root must adopt\nit explicitly with precedence over those two unqualified before-grant\nphrases, and over any reading of CONTRACT S6 or request acceptance that\nwould require the not-yet-created directory to have already been observed.\nThis is an explicit new policy for this branch, not silent inheritance of\nP213 authority and not completion of the old P212 B/S contracts.\n\n## One conditional staged grant\n\n1. Before issuing the new grant, root receives and binds the exact eight\n   adopted source bytes, whole V3 recipe/request, this supplement, the\n   selected P212 global runtime/content manifest, current relevant global\n   configuration/search binding, ordinary trusted-tool/namespace boundary,\n   controlled thirteen-variable environment, exact output pathname and\n   separately prepared/received output parent. Any known required resource\n   outside the received finite scope is resolved before grant. The P213\n   223-row list alone is not a completeness certificate. Source reception,\n   a manifest's existence, or the recipe's execution flag is not authority.\n2. A single separately issued root native grant may conditionally authorize\n   the exact V3 command. Initially it permits only its fixed preparation:\n   exclusive mkdir, manifests/content checks, eight-file copy/cmp/hash and\n   actual new-cwd guard. It does not assert these operations have succeeded\n   in advance. No existing/failed tree may be cleaned, resumed or reused.\n3. The TeX/BibTeX/rendering branch is authorized only if the preceding\n   operations and the in-command guard actually succeed. The guard must\n   record physical cwd and all dot-inclusive members of COLD and sections;\n   require the exact physical pathname, the exact 4/5 members and their\n   non-link ordinary file/directory types; reject texmf and .texlive2021\n   even as dangling links; and complete the subsequent product-absence\n   checks before the first TeX pass. A failed assertion exits under the\n   reviewed control flow. A new external observer or a root mid-command\n   acknowledgment is not required by this conditional policy.\n4. Completion of the command is not artifact acceptance. Root receives the\n   full actual native return/session sequence, raw controller/pass streams,\n   statuses and COLD_CWD.actual.txt, and independently checks the real cwd,\n   complete member records, guard-success marker and source/runtime guards.\n   The marker alone is insufficient. If launch/mkdir/redirection fails\n   before the EXIT trap is installed, retain the actual native failure;\n   do not invent a controller.exit or missing guard record.\n\nWithin this grant the recipe's existing ordinary /dev/null redirections,\n600-second build and 180-second PDF/page timeouts, TERM plus 10-second\nkill-after policy, fixed four passes and complete captures must be expressly\nwithin scope. A timeout/launch supervisor status is not an invented native\nTeX exit. Only the actual returned session may be continued; there is no\nsecond launch, automatic repair, retry or reuse of an old consumed grant.\n\n## What remains unchanged\n\nThe guard proves only the finite local facts actually recorded, under the\naccepted ordinary filesystem and namespace trust. It is not a hostile-race,\nancestor/descriptor, continuous-process or exhaustive installed-source\nattestation. The archived unset-HOME relative trees and TEXMFDOTDIR='.'\njustify its selected targets only with the separately received current\nglobal configuration binding; the guard does not establish that binding.\n\nEvery ordered FLS event, including duplicates and generated-file chronology,\nmust later be received against P212's own sources and manifest. Unknown\nconsumed input stops acceptance and grants no host-path follow, resource\ninstallation/generation or retry. Full logs, BibTeX AUX-before/BLG/BBL and\nall five keys, warnings/glyphs/fonts/text, actual page count, complete PNG\nset and actual all-page views remain necessary. No P213 counts or PDFs\ntransfer. Initial build, Round0, both nonauthor manuscript reviews and\ndeltas, required scientific/verifier gates, both terminal cold builds and\nfinal reception remain unwaived. HOLD_EXTERNAL remains.\n\nIndependent disposition: the staged policy above is technically coherent\nwith the exact reviewed V3 source. P212-POLICY-TIME1 can be closed by an\nexplicit root adoption of this precedence and staging; this document does\nnot claim that adoption has already happened.\n",
    "archived_contract": "# P212 plain-build replacement contract — PROPOSED, not adopted\n\nThis is a prospective P212 presentation/build branch, not an adapter into the old S0 interface. Independent SOURCE review and explicit root POLICY adoption are required. No existing source reception, DATA receipt, unresolved obligation, failed evidence or consumed grant is overwritten. No program in this package has been executed. The manuscript's mathematical assertions are not strengthened.\n\n## Exact presentation delta\n\nEight complete originals and eight complete proposed inputs accompany SOURCE.diff. Only main.tex and sections/02_returns.tex differ. The six other files, including references.bib and math_commands.tex, are byte-identical. Main changes article 10pt to 11pt, removes geometry/booktabs/array/fontenc/hyperref, retains amsmath/amssymb/amsthm, and adopts exactly P213's five kernel page dimensions. Main from input{math_commands} onward is unchanged. The table changes three booktabs rules to kernel hline and its three column specifications to kernel p columns of .42/.25/.25 linewidth. The table's explicit small command is also removed, retaining centering and ordinary body sizing. Every heading, cell, formula, theorem, proof, caption, label, reference and bibliography entry is unchanged. The entire changed table file is NOT byte-identical.\n\nKernel article supplies document/title/abstract/section/table/tabular/label/ref/cite/bibliography and p/@{} columns. AMS supplies theorem support, displayed alignment/cases/equation references/text fractions and blackboard symbols; the retained math_commands file supplies the existing custom macros. No remaining booktabs rule, array extension, geometry command or hyperref-specific command needs substitution. Removing hyperref loses clickable links/PDF metadata behavior, not reference text. Removing T1 switches back to the ordinary default encoding; no claim is made that the installed font graph follows from that statement. BibTeX plain and all five entries, including accent commands, remain unchanged. This is not a three-entry P213 bibliography. Font/glyph/resource and layout success require actual new evidence.\n\nNo display is pre-split; long displays are potential visual checks, not proven defects. Removing small eliminates that explicit small-table branch, but does not prove all subscript/font-size resources are covered. Table widths are a prospective layout choice, not proven to fit. No lmodern package or guessed metric filename is introduced.\n\n## Explicit trust boundary\n\nAdopt the P213 ordinary-tool boundary: trusted Bash/env, fixed TeX/BibTeX/PDF and filesystem tools, their ordinary installed configuration, namespace ancestors and transport. This explicitly withdraws from this NEW branch the old hostile-loader/installed-source correspondence, CRT/init-fini exhaustive closure, native14 descriptor/ancestor attestation, continuous own-process attestation, and no-unresolved-descendant-writer proof obligations. They are RETIRED-NOT-INVOKED/CLAIM-WITHDRAWN here, never PASS, and remain unresolved under their historical contracts. Applicable executable/library/configuration inputs are still real inputs; trust is not a fabricated exhaustive resource pin set.\n\nNo kpsewhich help/version/lookup, Python/Node preload/probe, seven-program old driver, ELF/package observer, ldd, generator, installer or source-correspondence operation is called by the proposed recipe. Existing accepted raw/ELF/cache/identity DATA remains archival evidence, not discarded or promoted to build authorization.\n\n## All seventeen old consumer dispositions (new branch only)\n\n| Old OBLIGATION_DELTA consumer, in original order | New branch disposition |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 CUDA alias observer/frontier/component keys | Not invoked; ordinary trusted ancestors plus finite content manifest replace build-side input guards, not native14 equivalence. |\n| 2 Python runtime probe/ctypes | Not invoked; no Python build controller. |\n| 3 Node runtime probe/native lazy bindings | Not invoked; any future DATA auditor is a separately reviewed trusted tool. |\n| 4 outer_contract descriptor/resolver/pre-Node keys | Not invoked; fixed source/request/manifest identities and actual artifact provenance replace its build role. |\n| 5 outer_contract subreaper/session/descendants | Claim withdrawn for new ordinary tool boundary; actual returned completion is not ECHILD or escaped-writer proof. |\n| 6 node_preload mapped keys/spawn events | Not invoked; exact shell argv/cwd/raw outputs do not become old native events. |\n| 7 driver STAT_KEYS/purpose guards/companions | Old schema rejected, not edited; recipe and request define a new build-only role. |\n| 8 keyed regular stdin/openStdin | Replaced explicitly by ordinary /dev/null redirection; no same-fd regular-EOF equivalence claimed. |\n| 9 product_capture/capture.js budgets and settlement | Not invoked; actual native request/session returns plus separate raw streams and supervisor statuses required. Ordinary timeout TERM and kill-after 10s are explicitly allowed only by a future new grant, unlike old no-signal branch. |\n| 10 DQD-O1/nonself binding | Meaning retained: independently receive exact external request/script/runtime manifest and fresh pre/post evidence; no self-declared hash or status grants authority. Old14 schema not imported. |\n| 11 trusted_product startup/provenance | New literal ordinary-tool trust decision required; old strict startup remains unsatisfied. |\n| 12 lookup options/53 proposals/returned sets | Entire kpsewhich query interface not invoked; no fictitious help/options/query results supplied. Finite resource/config facts must instead be independently received before build. |\n| 13 body pipeline/copy/cmp | Old body readers untouched/not called; new finite manifest and fresh source-only copies use ordinary trusted tools. No query-result-to-body capability is asserted. |\n| 14 S0 installed semantics prerequisite | Retired for absent query branch, not completed. New recipe's actual tool trust is explicit. |\n| 15 S1–S6 graphs and initial build plan | Replaced only as mapped below; resource/config coverage, fresh actual-cwd binding and complete artifacts remain required. |\n| 16 accepted author pair/runtime reuse | No science changes or science launch; reuse only after root confirms relevant dependencies unchanged. Presentation change does not automatically restart or certify science. |\n| 17 batch/manuscript/artifact gates | Entirely retained: initial build/all-page view, Round0, nonauthor A/B, required deltas/freezes/rounds, independent verifier/canonical pairs, two terminal cold builds and final artifact reception. Infrastructure review is not A/B. |\n\n## B and S obligations\n\nB1–B4 installed binary/source/loader/config/locale/initialization closure for the old S0 vectors are not proven. Their strict correspondence/hostile-loader claims are withdrawn for the uncalled branch; ordinary installed tool/config trust is proposed instead. B5 old policy is not expanded silently: this document requires NEW root adoption. B6 old keys/directories/raw/product reception remains historical and unsatisfied where unsatisfied; new build requires its own actual preparation, external binding, transport and artifact evidence.\n\nS0 query runtime/options is retired-not-invoked. S1 returned default/all/shadow body interface is retired; replacement is P212-specific finite resource identification and whole content pins before build, with no use of a failed FLS to discover new host inputs. S2 article10pt/eight-package graph is replaced by actual article11pt/AMS/kernel layout sources and the eight proposed document inputs. S3 T1 graph is retired only because T1 is removed; actual default-encoding text/math sizes, all five bibliography accents, metrics/maps/font programs still need relevant coverage. S4 exact format/config/search context remains a real received requirement under ordinary installed semantics, without claiming current latex.ltx proves compiled-format provenance. S5 native/render source closure is replaced by fixed ordinary trusted tools plus selected resource pins, not a complete ELF closure claim. S6 requires a fresh P212 manifest and relevant effective config/search/cwd binding in the actual new cold directory; old working-directory absences and P213's 223 pins cannot be transferred as completeness.\n\nThe 223 P213 entries are at most reusable candidates. Resource diagnosis lives separately in ../p212_plain_build_resource_diagnosis01/NOTE.md and is not automatically accepted by this contract. Missing/new relevant resources stop BEFORE build until separately identified and received. A later unknown FLS input stops acceptance, does not authorize reading that host path, repair, installation, generation or retry.\n\n## Prospective build and acceptance\n\nNATIVE_REQUEST.proposed.json supplies a fixed env -i with 13 variables, including SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1789084800 (explicitly changed from old P212 1788825600), openin/out_any=p, and all five MKTEX* generators disabled. It proposes Bash no-profile/no-rc and no shell escape. The script guard is not a grant; it may run only after exact source/policy/resource reception, fresh binding and a separate root native operation grant.\n\nThe output directory must be new and its parent separately prepared/received. No existing tree is cleaned or resumed. Copy only eight source inputs into a new source_only tree. Four passes: TeX/BibTeX/TeX/TeX. Preserve all before/after product presence/absence snapshots and complete raw stdout/stderr/supervisor exits. Timeout/launch status is not invented native TeX exit. Preserve every failed/partial tree and actual transport/session original; no automatic retry. No observer/import or host query occurs in this preparation.\n\nRoot must receive full logs, BLG/AUX/BBL and complete ordered FLS records including duplicates; classify actual input/output chronology and generated files across passes against the new manifest and source-only tree. Do not use old P213 event counts, 130-counterpart counts, three bibliography items or seven pages as P212 expectations. Receive actual reference/citation consistency, all five expected bibliography entries, warnings/missing glyphs/fonts, full PDF info/font/text output, actual page count, every rendered page and actual visual inspection. Hashes and diagnostic grep are not semantic/visual acceptance. Current proposal itself has no PDF/page/diagnostic result.\n\nThe recipe captures artifacts; it does not implement this later full artifact auditor, receive Round0, adopt a PDF or seal the paper. Two final independently cold builds and all manuscript gates remain later work. HOLD_EXTERNAL remains in force.\n\n## V3 fixed actual-cwd evidence (prospective)\n\nV3 keeps all eight V2 document inputs unchanged and adds only a Bash-builtin check after source-only copy/hash and before any TeX invocation. Under the same thirteen-variable environment, it records pwd -P, complete dotglob/nullglob member arrays for the cold directory and its sections child, and actual presence/absence of texmf and .texlive2021. Exactly three named root files plus the non-link sections directory and exactly five named non-link section files are required. Both relative trees must be absent even as dangling links; hence their texmf-config/texmf-var children cannot be local search trees. Full check source is pinned with the recipe; observed physical cwd and every enumerated member are written outside COLD in OUT/COLD_CWD.actual.txt before assertions. A final marker appears only after all exact membership/type/absence checks pass. Root must read actual evidence, not assume this proposal executed.\n\nThis supplies finite local-shadow/relative-tree absence evidence for archived TEXMFDOTDIR='.' and unset-HOME ./texmf and ./.texlive2021/{texmf-config,texmf-var}, subject to separately received current configuration binding. It does not query or independently assert unchanged effective host configuration. No parent/system directory is enumerated; no new kpsewhich, Node, host tool or manuscript edit is introduced. Failure preserves the new tree/evidence without repair/retry. Existing source-key checks are unchanged.\n\nArchived basis: ../p213_initial_build_runtime_resolution01/RUNTIME_NATIVE.json SHA256 d590b09facca16393f910d22b1c942a144fc933f02686a1447c125eeaa59af69, record p213rr_cnf__usr_share_texmf_web2c_texmf.cnf, plus that package's RUNTIME_SCOPE.json effective TEXMFHOME/TEXMFCONFIG/TEXMFVAR and TEXMFDOTDIR variables. See separately authored ../p212_plain_build_resource_diagnosis01/NOTE.md; this citation is not root acceptance or a new host observation.\n",
    "p214_source_reception": "# P214 display repair source adopted; ordinary staged policy accepted\n\nRoot received both complete initial DATA reports before adopting live source:\n../p214_initial_artifact_root01/RECEPTION.md retains HOLD and the six findings.\nThe exact repair PLAN/diff were reread at 6b4f22; complete final 163-line\nrecipe/request at 98a5b3. Independent SOURCE_ACCEPTABLE report and unchanged\nthree-payload seal were received previously; the complete four actual diff\ncomparisons were reread at 96c5b9. Root full source comparison 308ac0 verified\nall nine old sources and both physical proposal/originals before application.\nOnly sections/2_clock.tex and sections/5_scope.tex were then replaced with\nthe exact proposal bodies; all nine proposed hashes pass ab02d1. The old\noriginals and first cold tree remain physical unchanged evidence.\n\nThe product moves from inline to an unnumbered display without mathematical\nchange. The scope paragraph now states the actually accepted 5,271 states,\n10,646 records and two strict raw-identical replays, without upgrading finite\nevidence into proof/review. No other source, theorem, verifier, parameter,\nschema or canonical is changed. The new current source key is distinct;\nthe old 28-source manifest and all old seals remain historical, untouched.\n\nRoot explicitly adopts the same ordinary staged build policy as the initial\nP214 reception plus P212's STAGED_POLICY_SUPPLEMENT, reread in full 032b05.\nOnly paths/role labels and two source bodies change; four passes, nine\nsources, thirteen env variables, default AMS/plain resources and stage4/6\nmembership/absence guards remain. No new package/font/glyph consumer is\nintroduced. Current selected223 resource/configuration content and actual\nparent/capacity must be checked before a separate one-build grant.\nThe future cold cwd is checked after creation and before TeX, not invented\nbefore grant. No hostile loader or exhaustive tool/source closure is claimed.\n\nThis is source adoption and policy reception, not a build grant or repaired\nlayout verdict. Full new FLS/BibTeX/log/font/text and every page view must\nclose the initial overfull cause. No initial PDF adoption, Round0, A/B or\nterminal credit. HOLD_EXTERNAL.\n",
    "accepted_author_pair": "# P214 actual author strict pair accepted\n\n2026-09-11 UTC. ACCEPT_AUTHOR_STRICT_PAIR_UNCHANGED_SEMANTICS_REUSE.\nThis follows complete initial DATA reception in\n../p214_author_data_root01/RECEPTION.md and actual canonical adoption64394b.\nRoot re-read the complete final guard at e47932; its accepted source was\nunchanged. Actualb74091 freshly checked all68 initial keys including19\nruntime roles, allbytes and six metadata fields/zip ENOENT, canonical origin\nand absence of the two future grant/run paths. No runtime/key substitution.\n\nRoot separately issued and consumed GRANT.strict01.json then actually ran\nstrict01 atdba1e5,4.833878154s,exit0/no session. It then separately issued\nGRANT.strict02.json and ran strict02 atfe3e95,4.842904326s,exit0/no session.\nSTRICT01_NATIVE/STRICT02_NATIVE preserve exact requests and complete outputs.\nEach executed /usr/bin/python3.10 -I -S -B with absolute live verify.py,\ncwdworkspace, no scriptargs, envLANG=C/LC_ALL=C only, stdin/dev/null,\ncomplete file-backed stdout/stderr,600000ms SIGKILL timeout policy.\n\nActual4ec2ed independently checks both complete68-key PRE/POST snapshots,\nwholePREPOST RAW equality, zero errors/runtime metadata changes, all67\nshared complete keys equal to initial01, new exact grant/request/native\nand actual exit/pid, three request keys and both captured output keys.\nThree completeRAW comparisons pass: each10,419,112-byte stdout versus the\nactual canonical, and the two outputs against each other. Initial01 and\ncanonical are also fullRAW equal. All scientific streams have SHA256\n4ebeac267f855a1f9b03263ed2517d7a34b6dd0b62639b9fa54129c136763c35;\nboth stderr streams are empty. Full details in PAIR_NATIVE.json.\n\nExplicitly reuse accepted complete10646-record/all211105-comparison finite\nsemantics from the independentDATA+root replay under these unchanged bytes\nand full dependency keys. This is not a new DATA reconstruction or all-size\nproof. Both strict science executions are real; initial01 is not counted as\none of the pair. Nine original q/m boxes remain unchanged. sys remains a\nbuiltin import; no json dependency or canonical input was added.\n\nSource-era statements/28pins and original receipts remain historical;\ncanonical and these new receipts are additive roles, not rewritten history.\nThis closes author replay only. Source-only initial build/allpages/artifact,\nphysicalRound0, two distinct nonauthor manuscript reviews/deltas/freezes,\ntwo terminal builds and paper/batch gates remain mandatory.\nOWNER_AMBER/HOLD_EXTERNAL.\n",
    "paper_source_reception": "# P214 complete source and five-file amendment reception\n\n2026-09-11 UTC. ACCEPT_SOURCE_ONLY. No scientific execution or build.\nRoot has read all 28 original payloads, including the complete proof/manuscript,\n526-line original verifier, all output contracts, parameters, bibliography\nrecords and build plan. The admitted cancellation-safe clock, rectangle depth\ncensus, complete constructed inverse and explicit QMP/linear deductions remain\nunchanged. The fixed box is q,m in {2,3,4}; 5271 states and 10646 records are\nprospective, not observed. CANONICAL.json is explicitly permitted as the role\nname for complete JSONL, not one JSON object.\n\nRoot read the complete stable proposal NOTE, exact five-file diff and codec\ndomain proof (92d9a9), all 577-line proposed verifier (5a40ee/9dbb26), and all\nfour other full replacements (d5ddee). Its source SHA256 is\ndc1d9f73263e8330616b641ee89b0c22cfd5ab9dadb588664b50ca57fa67fb8b.\nAll 15 proposal payloads passed strict c0ba02. Accept the exact removal of json,\nbuiltin codec helpers and emit argument replacement, retaining sys, argv,\ntwo stdout writes, exceptions and every mathematical check. Code-point escape\npartition and structural induction establish equivalent JSON spelling on the\nexact acyclic builtin/string-key domain. This is deduction, not an executed\nserializer comparison or compatibility for arbitrary json inputs.\n\nAccept the two explicit h-domain manuscript clarifications, with no theorem\nchange. The application step must first physically preserve and compare the\nentire original 28-payload package plus its old seal, then apply only the five\nreviewed replacements and bind new current content separately. Old source\nhandoff/seal are historical and must not be rewritten as if they described the\nnew source. The proposal includes five complete original copies as well.\n\nRoot separately verified Bors's publisher Sections 1-2, Theorems 1-2 and their\nfinite-group hypotheses at https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00200-016-0304-9 .\nThe 2017 issue/2016 online-year distinction is supported by the saved actual\npublisher metadata and BibTeX. For the Fibonacci template, root read the\npublisher record and arXiv PDF introduction defining H_c=(xy+c,x):\nhttps://arxiv.org/pdf/1304.4864 . The publisher PDF web open was refused and\nthe separate stream e9acb0 returned empty-document failure; root does not\nclaim its own fresh published-page read. The source assistant's actual\npublished pp2449-2450 reading record remains the journal locator evidence;\nroot's independent formula reading is explicitly from the preprint. Neither\nsource supplies the finite-ring clock. Research-lit guided this bounded\nprimary-source distinction; no new bibliography or broad review was added.\n\nNext: exact application/current pins, then separately receive runtime guard\nand bind ordinary selected dependencies before any run. SOURCE acceptance is\nnot author numerical acceptance, Round0, A/B, paper completion or novelty\nclearance. All proof/code contributors remain ineligible to review P214.\nHOLD_EXTERNAL.\n",
    "accepted_author_data": "# P214 initial full scientific DATA accepted\n\n2026-09-11 UTC. ACCEPT_COMPLETE_INITIAL_DATA_SEMANTICS.\nRoot fullsource reception preceded both actual DATA invocations. Independent\ne54379 exited0/no session; rootdb7398 returned session14080 and actuald01957\ncontinued that same session to exit0. Exact requests/complete returns are\npreserved in DATA_NATIVE and DATA_CONTINUATION_NATIVE; all stderr is empty.\nRoot read full independent REPORT atb65bb4 and actual native/request at\n646b81, not just a delegated verdict. No scientific producer ran in this gate.\n\nRoot actual471980 compares all7,635,312 report bytes RAW-equal with the\nindependent output, SHA256\na10d0d5d973d51525fd6a057ef11704375fb330c3a62d68271cd0b4c077abaf8.\nThe actual full checker made381643 assertions and independently recomputed\nall211105 named producer comparisons, including exact condition multiplicity.\nAll10646 records passed complete expected payload, nested schema and exact\nASCII sorted-key wire, covering5271states/5271targets/9carriers, all literal\nF/L/M transitions, repeat-only clocks, complete inverse cosets, counts and\nwitnesses. This is a full finite-box semantic check, not an all-size proof.\n\nRoot471980 additionally rechecked every ledger row against the complete\n10,419,112-byte scientific stream and all63 current DATA-input whole bytes\nand six metadata fields. Full original capture initial01 remains actual\n9644b6 with raw SHA\n4ebeac267f855a1f9b03263ed2517d7a34b6dd0b62639b9fa54129c136763c35.\nThe root checker independently received all49 workspace capture keys plus\nthe archived19runtime comparison; that is not a new host observation.\nFull diagnostics/check registry and nine carrier summaries were read at\n2edd42. Original source4payload/56pins and final11payload seals passed;\nFINAL_SEAL_NATIVE records the final strict command. Wrong-cwd592419 remains\ndisclosed in SOURCE_RECEPTION, not a checker failure or strict success.\n\nRoot now permits exclusive canonical adoption of exactly initial01 stdout,\nwith wholeRAW comparison and unchanged source/runtime provenance. The role\nCANONICAL.json deliberately holds full JSONL, not a single JSON object.\nThis receipt does not itself copy it or authorize a science run. Two later\nstrict executions need new grants/current complete keys and raw comparisons;\nunchanged full semantics may be explicitly reused. No build/Round0/A/B or\npaper completion is asserted. OWNER_AMBER/HOLD_EXTERNAL.\n",
    "independent_repair_source_audit": "# P214 display/status repair — independent SOURCE audit\n\n2026-09-11 UTC. Reviewer `/root/p213_manuscript_review_a`.\n**SOURCE_ACCEPTABLE: 0 Critical / 0 Major / 0 Minor new open findings.**\nThe existing 19.01251pt layout finding is NOT closed by this source audit.\nActual adoption, fresh binding/grant, build, complete artifact reception and\nnew all-page views remain root's separate obligations.\n\nI am a nonauthor of P214 and of this repair proposal. I supplied no P214\nmathematical proof, verifier or proposed repair bytes. Prior P212/P213\nreview familiarity is disclosed; this is not blind or external review and\nearns no P214 manuscript-review credit. Only this audit directory is written.\nNo live edit, program parsing/import, DATA checker, science, TeX/build,\nruntime/host query or additional agent was used. Native diff/cmp/hash checks\nbelow are read-only documentary checks, not execution of proposed source.\n\n## Complete reviewed inputs\n\nThe complete PLAN, both complete original/proposed section pairs, all four\ndiffs, both nine-row placement manifests, complete 163-line shell recipe and\ncomplete native request were read. The complete original ordinary-policy\nreception, staged-policy supplement, V3 CONTRACT, P212 A source reception\nand P214 initial source/policy reception were read. The complete accepted\nP214 author DATA and strict-pair receipts were read, not just their titles.\nCurrent stream/batch headers were used only for navigation.\n\nThe preparation package's 15 payloads passed strict hashes at actual\n280710; its 15 workspace documentary input pins passed at 4684eb. The nine\nlive source files passed the BEFORE placement key at 479d71. Proposed\nplacement remains a future key, not a claim that live adoption occurred.\nThe two proposed section hashes match the two changed rows; all seven\nother rows and filenames are unchanged. No runtime-manifest target was\nfollowed: its documentary hash is not fresh resource acceptance.\n\nDIFF_NATIVE.json preserves this reviewer's exact requests and full native\nresults for all four whole-diff comparisons. Fresh `diff` output matches\nthe saved RECIPE, REQUEST, combined SOURCE and SOURCE_PINS diff files byte\nfor byte (actual 6476fb, 3e1b32, 570497, 0b8b6d; cmp exits 0). A diff's\nnormal changed-file status is not a build status. SOURCE_NATIVE.json is\nhistorical author provenance: its 1–170 lines and supplementary remainder\nwere inspected, but one long embedded request-diff display was truncated.\nI do not claim a complete manual reading of that embedded duplicate. The\nactual standalone request, diff and recipe were each read completely and\nthe whole diff independently compared above; no conclusion relies on the\ntruncated duplicate or its author-declared text-check booleans.\n\n## Two-file amendment\n\nIn sections/2_clock.tex the existing product\n`q^{\\lceil h/2\\rceil}q^{\\lfloor h/2\\rfloor}=q^h` is unchanged as a\nmathematical token sequence. Inline delimiters are replaced only by an\nunnumbered display and line breaks. All surrounding wording, theorem/proof\nstatements, labels and numbered equations are unchanged. The source adds\nno package, global layout/font declaration, spacing tolerance or mathematical\nassumption. This audit checks invariance, not the underlying theorem anew.\n\nIn sections/5_scope.tex the designed/not-executed historical wording becomes\nan actual finite-verification statement. The q,m boxes stay {2,3,4}; the\nq=4 field description and final limitations paragraph remain unchanged.\nThe new 5,271-state/nine-carrier and 10,646-record counts agree with the\naccepted full DATA receipt (381643 checker assertions, all 10646 records,\n5271 states and 5271 targets). The stated two *further* strict runs are\nsupported by the accepted strict01 dba1e5 and strict02 fe3e95, distinct from\ninitial01. That receipt records complete RAW comparisons with the actual\n10,419,112-byte canonical, SHA256\n4ebeac267f855a1f9b03263ed2517d7a34b6dd0b62639b9fa54129c136763c35.\nI reused those accepted receipts as evidence of past results; no new DATA\nreconstruction, stream comparison or scientific execution is claimed here.\n\nThe paragraph explicitly denies that finite checks establish the\nall-parameter statements. Neither replacement claims manuscript A/B,\ncompletion, broader rings, new all-time fibres or novelty. Updating this\nlive-stage account does not authorize alteration of frozen source-era\ndocuments or their seals.\n\n## Recipe, request and policy continuity\n\nThe complete recipe differs from the accepted initial recipe only in its\nadoption comment, preparation/binding/output paths and supervisor label.\nThe source root remains the same live paper, but only AFTER root separately\npreserves/compares the originals and adopts exactly the two proposed files.\nThe native request agrees with the recipe's new preparation path, new\n`p214_display_repair_binding01` and exclusive `p214_display_repair_run01`.\nThe new schema/status labels do not reuse an initial-build grant or output.\n`operation_authorized=false` and null actual-adoption/grant/runtime fields\ncorrectly describe preparation, not execution.\n\nThe command-line flag is only an invocation guard, not authentication or\nauthority. Root's separate exact source/request/policy/resource grant is\nstill essential. Runtime candidate223 is expressly archival. Current full\nselected bytes, relevant global configuration, ordinary tool/namespace/\ntransport trust, output parent and capacity must be received before grant.\nThe old hostile-loader/B/S/init/continuous-process claims remain withdrawn\nor retired-not-invoked, not passed by this adaptation.\n\nThe thirteen explicit environment variables, isolated no-profile/no-rc Bash,\nno shell escape, five disabled MKTEX generators, /dev/null input, four\nTeX/BibTeX/TeX/TeX passes, 600-second build and 180-second PDF/page bounds,\nTERM plus 10-second kill-after and eight product snapshots are unchanged.\nThe fixed nine source files are copied/cmp/hash checked into a new tree;\nold PDF/AUX/BBL/BLG/FLS/LOG, canonical and verifier are not cold inputs.\n\nThe accepted staged timing remains coherent: exclusive creation/copy/hash\nprecedes the actual physical-cwd and dot-inclusive 4-root/6-section member\nchecks. Exact allowed names, non-link ordinary types, relative texmf and\n.texlive2021 absence (including dangling links) and initial product absence\nare required before any TeX pass. Future directory facts are not asserted\npre-creation. A failed early mkdir/redirection may lack controller.exit;\nthe native failure must be retained rather than an exit invented.\n\nThe recipe captures complete streams and supervisor results, records all\neight before/after product sets, checks source/runtime keys and renders\nevery actual page at 150 dpi. It does not itself establish semantic FLS,\nfont/glyph/reference/layout acceptance. The request correctly retains the\nfull ordered FLS/generated chronology and AUX-before/BLG/BBL bibliography\nreconciliation requirement. No old event counts or bibliography roles are\ntransferred. Unexpected consumed inputs stop acceptance, with no host-path\nfollow, install, retry or cleanup authorized. A 4–6-page target is intent,\nnot an observed or hardcoded actual page count.\n\n## Findings and next boundary\n\nNo source correction is requested. The archived 19.01251pt overflow remains\nan OPEN artifact concern until the actual repaired build's full logs and\nall newly rendered pages are received and viewed, including any repagination\nand the new printed results paragraph. This audit did not view a proposed\nrepair PDF (none is produced by this task), nor claim that display syntax\nguarantees visual closure. The original artifact is preserved.\n\nRoot may now independently read and receive this exact proposal/audit,\ndecide precise live adoption and bind one new conditional staged build.\nThis report supplies no build grant, PDF adoption, Round0/A/B/terminal or\npaper-completion credit. HOLD_EXTERNAL remains. The project skill's\naffected-dependency rule kept this review limited to the display/status\ndelta and its actual evidence/policy dependencies.\n\n## Pin and seal roles\n\nINPUT_PINS.sha256 is workspace-root-relative. Its exact preparation seal\ntransitively binds ALL 15 preparation payloads, including both complete\nbefore/proposed sections, recipe/request/diffs/native record and placement\nkeys. The pinned preparation INPUT_PINS binds its 15 original documentary\ninputs; these were all hash checked, not recursively treated as host keys.\nBoth pinned placement files specify the complete nine-source inventories.\nThe two additional policy originals not in that preparation input list are\ndirectly pinned here. This explicitly nested pin closure avoids copying or\nresealing historical artifacts; it is not an incomplete main-script-only key.\nOur directory-relative SHA256SUMS covers all three audit payloads and\nexcludes itself. No final manuscript manifest is asserted.\n"
